alpine-baselayout — installed as: alpine-baselayout, alpine-baselayout-data
Licence declared by Alpine: GPL-2.0-only

The base directory layout and the default files under /etc. /etc/protocols and /etc/services come from Debian's netbase, which is also under the GPL, version 2.

Written by the Alpine Linux project. It has no upstream source: its source is the aport
itself, https://gitlab.alpinelinux.org/alpine/aports/-/tree/3.24-stable/main/alpine-baselayout, which contains no licence file and no copyright notice. Alpine declares
GPL-2.0-only for it, and no copyright notice has been published for it, so none is reproduced here.

The GPL, version 2, is a standard text and needs no copyright notice of its own to state it,
so it is reproduced alongside as GPL-2.0-only.txt, from SPDX's licence list.
